@startuml dp-self-installation
title A data product installing and registering itself (via the control center)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Cindy\n(engineer)" as CINDY
participant "Sidecar" as SC
participant "Control center\n(hub)" as CC
participant "Source control\n(ODPS, ODCS, SBOM)" as SCM
participant "System\n(servers, storage,\npipeline)" as SYS
participant "Marketplace" as MP
actor "Users\n(Juliette, Beth...)" as USERS

CINDY -> SC : install & deploy sidecar

== Boot ==
SC -> CC : request own descriptors
CC -> SCM : fetch (contract is source of truth)
SCM --> CC : ODPS, ODCS, SBOM
CC --> SC : descriptors
note over SC, SCM : The sidecar never talks to source control directly. The control center or the marketplace is the hub.
SC -> SYS : locate & connect components\nfrom the server block
SC -> SC : start the data product

== Register (architecture choice) ==
alt Sidecar registers directly
  SC -> MP : OOCS register
  MP --> SC : OORS ack
else Control center brokers the registration
  SC -> CC : OOCS register
  CC -> MP : forward register
  MP --> CC : OORS ack
  CC --> SC : ack
end

@enduml